*hendecasyllable* (Pros.); 'eleven-syllable'. Applicable, & occasionally applied, to any metre having lines of eleven syllables, e.g. to Dante's terza rima; but so far appropriated to what is called in full *the Phalaecian h.* that to use it of other metres risks misunderstanding. The P.h. is the Greek & Latin metre best known from Catullus, having the scheme —⏙/—⏑⏑/—⏑/—⏑/—⏙, & imitated by Tennyson:—
===
